## Where the cycle paused

Just completed `src/.aide` body. Standing by for user decision on the
batching strategy for the remaining ~24 specs. Four options surfaced (per
the conversation):

- **A.** Per-spec approval each cycle (~24 cycles).
- **B.** Batch by depth — spawn all rewriters at the same depth in
  parallel, present the depth as a bundle, land in bulk, descend
  (~4-5 cycles).
- **C.** Spawn everything in parallel, single bulk review at the end
  (~1-2 cycles).
- **D.** Hybrid — per-spec approval for wholesale rewrites
  (`src/cli/init/.aide`, `src/service/install/.aide`,
  `src/service/install/provisionBrain/.aide`,
  `src/service/parseBrainAide/.aide`); bulk approval per-depth for
  trim-only specs (~7-8 cycles).

Recommended: **D**. Awaiting user choice.

