1. **Maintainer agent design.** Trigger (`/aide:maintain` user-invoked
   vs. scheduled), autonomy (auto-delete vs. flag-for-review), what
   signals "dead" (all checkboxes done + git commit landed + age
   threshold + explicit user marking). Defer until the bloat sweep
   finishes; then design and ship.
2. **Brain-layer parent spec.** Aligner suggested an intermediate
   parent for brain doctrine; rejected this cycle in favor of
   push-to-leaves (no common subdirectory). Re-evaluate if leaf-level
   sibling-redundancy persists after this sweep.
3. **`.aide/handoff.aide` content disposition.** The brain-rework state
   summary that USED to live in handoff.aide has been absorbed into
   this file as anti-regression invariants 1-28. The retro from that
   cycle should be promoted to brain at `process/retro/` before this
   `session.aide` is eventually deleted (when the spec-bloat refactor
   feature closes). Not yet promoted.

