## Process discipline (permanent)

- Every fresh agent reads this file before acting in this repo.
- Two methodology-mandated pause points stay unconditional regardless
  of mode: after spec-writer returns frontmatter (Stage 1) and after
  architect returns `plan.aide` (Stage 4) — present to user, wait for
  explicit approval before advancing.
- One implementor per numbered plan step, fresh context each time.
- The orchestrator NEVER writes substantive files itself; it delegates
  every phase to the appropriate specialized agent. Direct edits to
  `.claude/` files (agent definitions, command prompts, skill prompts)
  ARE allowed because those are the agent runtime, not pipeline
  artifacts.
- `.aide/docs/`, `.aide/intent.aide`, `.aide/config/brain.aide`, and
  `.aide/session.aide` ARE pipeline-appropriate when their updates
  ride alongside a code amendment.
